				"README.md": {
					"diff": "--- published/README.md\n+++ rebuilt/README.md\n@@ -1,17 +1,572 @@\n-# VSCode Language Server - Client Module\n+# VSCode Language Server - Node\n \n+This repository contains the code for the following npm modules:\n+\n+\n+* _vscode-languageclient_: npm module to talk to a VSCode language server from a VSCode extension:<br>\n [![NPM Version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/vscode-languageclient.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageclient)\n [![NPM Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/vscode-languageclient.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageclient)\n-[![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/Microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/Microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node)\n+* _vscode-languageserver_: npm module to implement a VSCode language server using [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) as a runtime:<br>\n+[![NPM Version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/vscode-languageserver.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver)\n+[![NPM Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/vscode-languageserver.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver)\n+* _vscode-languageserver-textdocument_: npm module to implement text documents usable in a LSP server using [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) as a runtime:<br>\n+[![NPM Version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/vscode-languageserver-textdocument.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver-textdocument)\n+[![NPM Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/vscode-languageserver-textdocument.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver-textdocument)\n+* _vscode-languageserver-protocol_: the actual language server protocol definition in TypeScript:<br>\n+[![NPM Version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/vscode-languageserver-protocol.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver-protocol)\n+[![NPM Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/vscode-languageserver-protocol.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver-protocol)\n+* _vscode-languageserver-types_: data types used by the language server client and server:<br>\n+[![NPM Version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/vscode-languageserver-types.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver-types)\n+[![NPM Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/vscode-languageserver-types.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-languageserver-types)\n+* _vscode-jsonrpc_: the underlying message protocol to communicate between a client and a server:<br>\n+[![NPM Version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/vscode-jsonrpc.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-jsonrpc)\n+[![NPM Downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/vscode-jsonrpc.svg)](https://npmjs.org/package/vscode-jsonrpc)\n+\n+All npm modules are built using one Azure Pipeline. Its status is:\n+\n+[![Build Status](https://dev.azure.com/vscode/vscode-languageserver-node/_apis/build/status%2Fvscode-languageserver-node?branchName=main)](https://dev.azure.com/vscode/vscode-languageserver-node/_build/latest?definitionId=52&branchName=main)\n+\n+Click [here](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/extensions/example-language-server) for a detailed document on how to use these npm modules to implement\n+language servers for [VSCode](https://code.visualstudio.com/).\n \n-This npm module allows VSCode extensions to easily integrate langauge servers adhering to the [language server protocol](https://github.com/Microsoft/vscode-languageserver-protocol)\n+## Contributing\n \n-See [here](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/extensions/example-language-server) for a detailed documentation on how to \n-implement language servers for [VSCode](https://code.visualstudio.com/).\n+After cloning the repository, run `npm install` to install dependencies and `npm run symlink` to point packages in this repository to each other.\n+\n+See [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for the repository map, focused build and test commands, generated-file workflows, and maintenance hazards. AI coding agents should also read [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md).\n \n ## History\n \n-For the history please see the [main repository](https://github.com/Microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/blob/master/README.md)\n+## 3.18.6 Protocol, 10.0.1 JSON-RPC, 11.0.1 Client and 11.0.1 Server.\n+\n+[Fixed issues](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20is%3Aclosed%20reason%3Acompleted%20milestone%3A%223.18.6%22%20sort%3Aupdated-desc) | [Merged pull requests](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/pulls?q=is%3Apr%20is%3Amerged%20milestone%3A%223.18.6%22%20sort%3Aupdated-desc)\n+\n+### Compatibility\n+\n+- No protocol requests, notifications, or responses changed. The protocol package is a patch release with updated JSON-RPC and types dependencies.\n+- Client: when initialization is retried through `initializationFailedHandler` or the Retry message of an `InitializeError`, `start()` now resolves or rejects with the outcome of the last attempt. For a retryable `InitializeError` without a handler, `start()` stays pending until the user answers the Retry message.\n+- Client: document formatting requests now forward additional formatting options provided by VS Code to the server.\n+- Type guards in the types and protocol packages now return `false` for `null`, `undefined`, and other non-object values instead of throwing.\n+- Text document 1.0.16 is unchanged.\n+\n+### Bug fixes and improvements\n+\n+- Client: dispose workspace diagnostic progress handlers on all paths, skip workspace diagnostic reports that fail to convert, report the correct failed request, and reset the error counter after a successful workspace pull.\n+- Client: refresh dependent notebook cell diagnostics after text changes and cancel pending change deliveries when the client stops.\n+- JSON-RPC 10.0.1: `LinkedMap.delete` and `LRUCache.delete` now return `true` for existing falsy values.\n+- Protocol 3.18.6: `NotebookDocumentFilter.is` accepts relative patterns.\n+- Server: only track server-created work done progress reporters and ignore failed progress sends.\n+- Types 3.18.6: keep existing change annotations when `WorkspaceChange` wraps a `WorkspaceEdit`.\n+\n+## 3.18.5 Protocol, 10.0.0 JSON-RPC, 11.0.0 Client and 11.0.0 Server.\n+\n+[Fixed issues](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20is%3Aclosed%20reason%3Acompleted%20milestone%3A%223.18.5%22%20sort%3Aupdated-desc) | [Merged pull requests](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/pulls?q=is%3Apr%20is%3Amerged%20milestone%3A%223.18.5%22%20sort%3Aupdated-desc)\n+\n+### Compatibility\n+\n+- JSON-RPC now requires Node.js 14.17.0 or newer.\n+- The exported `PipeTransport` and `SocketTransport` interfaces now require a `close()` method to release listeners when a server fails before connecting. The built-in transport factories provide this method. These interfaces are also re-exported by the client and server Node.js entry points.\n+- UUID generation is centralized in the JSON-RPC runtime abstraction layer. `RAL` is implemented by the npm module; external implementations are not supported.\n+- No protocol requests, notifications, or responses changed. The protocol package remains a patch release with updated JSON-RPC and types dependencies.\n+\n+### Bug fixes and improvements\n+\n+- Client: fix startup and shutdown failures, connection-close races, and cleanup when a server process exits before connecting.\n+- Client: preserve document-open notification ordering, dispose duplicate file-watcher registrations, and avoid relying on `Promise.prototype.finally` during startup and shutdown.\n+- Client: allow diagnostic pulls to recover after failures and refresh notebook diagnostics after cell reordering.\n+- JSON-RPC: release parallel dispatch slots after rejected messages, fire missing IPC writer and port reader close events, and correct buffer slicing.\n+- Server: remove deleted notebook cells from the cell map and avoid Windows command-spawning deprecation warnings.\n+- Types 3.18.5: correct the `ColorPresentation.is` and `FoldingRange.is` type guards.\n+- Text document 1.0.16: correct line offsets when incremental edits form CRLF across edit boundaries.\n+\n+## 3.18.4 Protocol, 9.0.3 JSON-RPC, 10.1.2 Client and 10.1.2 Server.\n+\n+[Bug fixes and small improvements](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/issues?q=is%3Aclosed%20milestone%3A%223.18.4%22)\n+\n+\n+## 3.18.3 Protocol, 9.0.1 JSON-RPC, 10.1.1 Client and 10.1.1 Server.\n+\n+[Bug fixes and small improvements](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-languageserver-node/issues?q=is%3Aclosed%20milestone%3A%223.18.3%22)\n+\n+\n",
